  "note": "Recorded against the NovEx WarehouseCraft test account. The documented api/OrderStatus/ByDate route answers 404 on the tenant; the tenant speaks /api/OrderStatusDatas?startDate=&endDate= (date-only bounds are inclusive by calendar day; datetime bounds without a zone designator are honoured to the second in the server's local clock, which trails UTC by 5 hours in the ImportDate column) plus /api/OrderStatusDatas/{OrderId} and ?clientOrderId=. No order on the test account has shipped; the by_id_foreign_order call (OrderId 1, another client's 2019 ISC test order that the tenant returned for a bare numeric id) is the only LIVE shipped row: its ShippingData carries ShipDate, Carrier, TrackingNumber, PalletCount, WeightInLbs, UCC128 and NO DeliverDate/TrackingStatus keys, matching the 3PL's note that this API does not report delivered. The published schema (doc_sample) also lists DeliverDate, TrackingStatus and TrackingDeliveryExceptions; the parser reads them when present. Because by-id answers for ids outside our account, every by-id read must be matched on ClientOrderId before it is trusted.",
